#: ../../../contributing.rst:2
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:1
msgid ""
"So you’d like to contribute? Awesome! Here are some things worth knowing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:5
msgid "Reporting a bug / requesting a feature / asking a question"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:7
msgid ""
"Go `open an issue <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/issues>`_ or `start a "
"discussion <https://github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/discussions>`_ and I’ll "
"probably reply soon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:10
msgid "Contributing to the docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:12
msgid ""
"Just make a PR with your proposed changes targeting the main branch. The "
"`documentation website <https://poethepoet.natn.io/>`_ will update once your "
"PR is merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:15
msgid "Contributing code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:18
msgid "Preface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:20
msgid ""
"If you’re willing to contribute your ideas and effort to making poethepoet "
"better, then that’s awesome and I’m grateful. I don’t have all the answers "
"so it’s particularly important for this project to benefit from diverse "
"perspectives and technical expertise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:22
msgid ""
"However please be aware that a lot of thought has gone into the architecture "
"of poethepoet, and whilst I know it’s not perfect, and I am very interested "
"in alternative perspectives, I do have strong (and I hope reasonable) "
"opinions about how certain things should work. This particularly applies to "
"naming and internal APIs. There is a lot to consider in terms of making sure "
"the tool stays simple, flexible, and performant. So please don’t be offended "
"if there is some push back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:25
msgid "Development process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:27
msgid ""
"If your planned changes entail non-trivial UI or internal API changes then "
"it’s a good idea to bring them up for discussion as a `GitHub issue <https://"
"github.com/nat-n/poethepoet/issues>`_ first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:29
msgid ""
"Fork and clone the repo, and create a feature or bugfix branch off of the "
"*development* branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:31
msgid ""
"Double check that you’re starting from the *development* branch, and not "
"from the the *main* branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:33
msgid ""
"Run ``poetry install`` to setup your development environment. (`install "
"poetry <https://python-poetry.org/docs/#installation>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:35
msgid ""
"The ``poe schema-build`` task — also invoked by ``poe check`` via ``poe "
"schema-check-drift`` — postprocesses the generated JSON Schema with prettier "
"(run through ``npx``). This requires `Node.js <https://nodejs.org>`__ on "
"your PATH. Install Node.js if you plan to touch anything that affects schema "
"generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:37
msgid "Do your code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:39
msgid ""
"If you’ve added a feature then before it can be including in a release we "
"will need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:41
msgid "a feature test along the same lines as the examples in the tests dir,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:42
msgid "to update documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:44
msgid ""
"Run ``poe check`` to check that you haven’t broken anything that will block "
"the CI pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:46
msgid ""
"Create a commit with a clear commit message that describes the commit "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:48
msgid "Open a PR on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:52
msgid ""
"You can also open a draft PR proposing incomplete changes to recieve "
"feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:55
msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:57
msgid ""
"There isn’t currently a pull request template, but please try and be "
"descriptive about what problem you’re solving and how, and reference related "
"issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:59
msgid ""
"In some cases it might be acceptable to merge code to *development* to make "
"a pre-release from it without including full automated tests and "
"documentation. However this is a special case, because it blocks further "
"releases from the *development* branch until the tests and docs are there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:63
msgid "Branching model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:65
msgid "This project implements something like git flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:67
msgid ""
"*TL;DR* branch off of *development* for new features, or *main* for "
"documentation improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:69
msgid ""
"We like to keep a clean history, so squash-rebase merges are preferred for "
"the *development* or *main* branches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:72
msgid "Overview of branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:75
msgid "Historic branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:77
msgid ""
"**main** the primary branch containing released code and up to date docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:78
msgid ""
"**development** in progress and pre-released features that are expected to "
"be included in a release when ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:81
msgid "Working branches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:83
msgid "**hotfix/** branches for minor/urgent bug fixes from main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:84
msgid "**feature/** branches for new feature development from development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:85
msgid "**bugfix/** for new bug fixes from development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:86
msgid "**doc/** branches for documentation changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:89
msgid "How to add a new feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:91
msgid "Create your branch from *development*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:93
msgid ""
"git fetch\n"
"git checkout origin/development\n"
"git checkout -b feature/my_new_feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:99
msgid "Create a pull request back to *development*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:102
msgid "How to add a hot fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:104
msgid "Create your branch from *main*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:106
msgid ""
"git fetch\n"
"git checkout origin/main\n"
"git checkout -b feature/my_new_feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:112
msgid "Create a pull request back to *main*, and one to *development*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:115
msgid "How to create release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:117
msgid ""
"From the head of the *development* branch, use the ``bump-version`` poe task "
"to bump the version, then commit the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:118
msgid ""
"Create a release (and tag) on GitHub, following the existing convention for "
"naming and release notes format (use the *Generate release notes* button as "
"a starting point), and the GitHub CI will do the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../.github/CONTRIBUTING.rst:119
msgid ""
"Unless it is a pre-release then the final step is to merge *development* "
"into *main*."
msgstr ""
